{=============================================================================
  Air-cooled heat exchanger, air side: finned-tube-bundle heat-transfer
  coefficient, air-side pressure drop and fan noise (function library)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0099 (function library, kind = function)
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Eight correlations of the air side of an air cooler (a finned tube bundle
  crossed by air), all of them taken from the Python library ht:

    - the air-side heat-transfer coefficient on a bare-tube basis, with the
      Briggs and Young formula, the ESDU high-fin and low-fin formulas and the
      Ganguli/VDI formula (four functions);
    - the air-side pressure drop across the bundle, with the ESDU high-fin and
      low-fin formulas (two functions);
    - the sound pressure level of an air-cooler bay with one fan, with the
      GPSA and the Mukherjee formulas (two functions).

  Every heat-transfer and pressure-drop function is the *product* of a
  dimensionless correlation and of the surface geometry: the caller passes the
  mass flow rate of air, the minimum free-flow area, the areas and pitches of
  the bundle and the air properties, as in the original library. No air
  property is evaluated here: rho, Cp, mu, k and k_fin are inputs.

  Two helpers are needed by the four heat-transfer functions: the Kern and
  Kraus efficiency of a circular fin (with the modified Bessel functions
  I0, I1, K0 and K1 of its closed-form solution) and the two Bessel functions
  themselves, evaluated here by their power series because CoolSolve has no
  Bessel function (the same approach as CSL-0090). The row-count correction
  factor of the ESDU low-fin formula is written inline, with the table of
  CSL-0095 (ESDU_tube_row_correction), so that no function of another model is
  duplicated here.

  The demonstration program at the end calls every function: case A uses the
  input sets of the ht doctests, case B a second, uniform set (a two-row
  in-line low-fin bundle and a second fan). The ht values of both cases are
  tabulated in the README (verification table).

  Inputs : m [kg/s], A, A_min, A_fin, A_tube_showing [m^2], A_increase [-],
           tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, fin_height, bare_length,
           pitch_parallel, pitch_normal [m], tube_rows [-],
           flow_area_contraction_ratio [-], rho [kg/m^3], Cp [J/kg-K],
           mu [Pa-s], k [W/m-K], k_fin [W/m-K], Pr_wall [-],
           tip_speed [m/s], power [W], fan_diameter [m], induced [-]
  Outputs: h [W/m^2-K], dP [Pa], noise [dB(A)]
  Units  : SI - SI-MASS-DEG-PA-C-J (no unit conversion was needed: ht is SI)
  Source : ht (Caleb Bell), ht/air_cooler.py, version 1.2.0, commit 85e0ee6,
           MIT - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht ; correlations by the authors
           cited in each function block - see README.md
  Status : VERIFIED against the doctests and the values of ht 1.2.0
           (README.md, "Verification")
=============================================================================}

FUNCTION bessel_mod_I_series(n_order, z)
{BESSEL_MOD_I_SERIES - modified Bessel function of the first kind I_n(z), of
order 0 or 1, evaluated by its power series [-].

  I_n(z) = (z/2)^n sum_{k>=0} (z^2/4)^k / [k! (k+n)!]

Written with the terms a_k = (z^2/4)^k/(k!)^2, so that I_0 = sum a_k and
I_1 = (z/2) sum a_k/(k+1); the series is truncated after 13 terms
(k = 0..12). n_order is 0 or 1 [-], z > 0 [-].
Validity: the truncated series is exact to machine precision for z <= 2
  (the neglected term is below 1E-20 relative there); for larger z more terms
  are needed. The demonstration program stays below z = 1.7.
Original: Watson, G. N., "A Treatise on the Theory of Bessel Functions", 2nd
  edition, Cambridge University Press, 1945 (the series of the modified
  Bessel functions of the first kind, section 6.6); as given in Abramowitz,
  A. A. and I. F. Stegun, "Handbook of Mathematical Functions", 9th edition,
  Dover, 1964, formula 9.6.2.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/core.py, fin_efficiency_Kern_Kraus
  (which calls the modified Bessel functions I0 and I1 of the scipy library),
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  q = z^2/4
  a = 1
  S = 1
  T = 1
  DUPLICATE k = 1, 12
    a = a*q/(k*k)
    S = S + a
    T = T + a/(k+1)
  END
  IF n_order = 0 THEN
    bessel_mod_I_series = S
  ELSE
    bessel_mod_I_series = z/2*T
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION bessel_mod_K_series(n_order, z)
{BESSEL_MOD_K_SERIES - modified Bessel function of the second kind K_n(z), of
order 0 or 1, evaluated by its power series [-].

  K_0(z) = -[ln(z/2) + gamma] I_0(z) + sum_{k>=1} H_k (z^2/4)^k/(k!)^2

  K_1(z) = I_0(z)/z + [ln(z/2) + gamma] I_1(z) - (2/z) sum_{k>=1} k H_k a_k

with H_k the harmonic numbers (H_0 = 0), gamma = 0.577215664901533 the
Euler-Mascheroni constant and a_k = (z^2/4)^k/(k!)^2; I_0 and I_1 are the
truncated sums of bessel_mod_I_series, computed in the same loop. K_1 is the
negative derivative of K_0 (dI_0/dz = I_1, da_k/dz = 2k a_k/z), the form in
which the derivative of the series of K_0 can be written term by term. The sums
are truncated after 13 terms (k = 0..12).
n_order is 0 or 1 [-], z > 0 [-].
Validity: exact to machine precision for z <= 2 (the neglected term is below
  1E-20 relative there); for larger z more terms are needed. The
  demonstration program stays below z = 1.7.
Original: Watson, G. N., "A Treatise on the Theory of Bessel Functions", 2nd
  edition, Cambridge University Press, 1945; as given in Abramowitz, A. A. and
  I. F. Stegun, "Handbook of Mathematical Functions", 9th edition, Dover, 1964,
  formula 9.6.11 (differentiated term by term for K_1).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/core.py, fin_efficiency_Kern_Kraus
  (which calls the modified Bessel functions K0 and K1 of the scipy library),
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  q = z^2/4
  gamma = 0.577215664901533
  a = 1
  H = 0
  I_0 = 1
  I_1_sum = 1
  S_0 = 0
  S_1 = 0
  DUPLICATE k = 1, 12
    a = a*q/(k*k)
    H = H + 1.0/k
    I_0 = I_0 + a
    I_1_sum = I_1_sum + a/(k+1)
    S_0 = S_0 + H*a
    S_1 = S_1 + k*H*a
  END
  I_1 = z/2*I_1_sum
  IF n_order = 0 THEN
    bessel_mod_K_series = -(LN(z/2) + gamma)*I_0 + S_0
  ELSE
    bessel_mod_K_series = I_0/z + (LN(z/2) + gamma)*I_1 - 2*S_1/z
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler(tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, k_fin, h)
{ETA_FIN_KERN_KRAUS_AIRCOOLER - efficiency of a circular fin of constant
thickness attached to a circular tube [-]; the helper the four air-side
heat-transfer coefficients need.

  eta_f = 2 r_o / [m (r_e^2 - r_o^2)] *
          [I_1(m r_e) K_1(m r_o) - K_1(m r_e) I_1(m r_o)] /
          [I_0(m r_o) K_1(m r_e) + I_1(m r_e) K_0(m r_o)]

  m = sqrt(2 h/(k_fin t_fin)),  r_e = D_fin/2,  r_o = D_tube/2

tube_diameter [m] is the outer diameter of the bare tube, fin_diameter [m] the
outer diameter of the tube including its fins, fin_thickness [m] the fin
thickness, k_fin [W/m-K] the fin conductivity and h [W/m^2-K] the heat-transfer
coefficient on the fin surface. I_n and K_n are the modified Bessel functions
of bessel_mod_I_series and bessel_mod_K_series (CoolSolve has no Bessel
function, so they are evaluated here by their power series; the combination
below is the closed form of the original, unchanged).
Validity: no limits quoted in the original; the series form used for the Bessel
  functions is exact to machine precision for m r_e <= 2 (m r_e is 1.6 at most
  in the demonstration program).
Original: Kern, D. Q. and A. D. Kraus, "Extended Surface Heat Transfer",
  McGraw-Hill, 1972 (the exact efficiency of a circular fin of constant
  thickness); the same solution in Bergman, T. L., A. S. Lavine, F. P.
  Incropera and D. P. DeWitt, "Introduction to Heat Transfer", 6th edition,
  Wiley, 2011, and Thulukkanam, K., "Heat Exchanger Design Handbook", 2nd
  edition, CRC Press, 2013.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/core.py, fin_efficiency_Kern_Kraus,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  r_e = fin_diameter/2
  r_o = tube_diameter/2
  m = SQRT(2*h/(k_fin*fin_thickness))
  z_e = m*r_e
  z_o = m*r_o
  I1_z_e = bessel_mod_I_series(1, z_e)
  I1_z_o = bessel_mod_I_series(1, z_o)
  K1_z_e = bessel_mod_K_series(1, z_e)
  K1_z_o = bessel_mod_K_series(1, z_o)
  I0_z_o = bessel_mod_I_series(0, z_o)
  K0_z_o = bessel_mod_K_series(0, z_o)
  eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler = 2*r_o/(m*(r_e^2 - r_o^2))*(I1_z_e*K1_z_o - K1_z_e*I1_z_o)/(I0_z_o*K1_z_e + I1_z_e*K0_z_o)
END

FUNCTION h_Briggs_Young(m, A, A_min, A_increase, A_fin, A_tube_showing, tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, bare_length, rho, Cp, mu, k, k_fin)
{H_BRIGGS_YOUNG - air-side heat-transfer coefficient of a finned tube bundle
(a tube finned on both sides), as a bare-tube-basis coefficient (as if there
were no fins) [W/m^2-K].

  Nu = 0.134 Re^0.681 Pr^0.33 (S/h_f)^0.2 (S/t_f)^0.1134

  V_max = m/(A_min rho),  Re = V_max D_tube rho/mu,  Pr = Cp mu/k
  h = k/D_tube Nu
  h_{A,total} = (eta_f A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A h
  h_{bare,total} = A_increase h_{A,total}

m [kg/s] is the mass flow rate of air across the bundle, A [m^2] the combined
finned and bare surface area exposed, A_min [m^2] the minimum free-flow area,
A_increase [-] the ratio of the actual surface area to the bare-tube surface
area, A_fin [m^2] the area of all the fins, A_tube_showing [m^2] the area of
bare tube showing, tube_diameter [m] the bare-tube diameter, fin_diameter [m]
the tube diameter including its fins (fin height h_f = (fin_diameter -
tube_diameter)/2), fin_thickness [m] the fin thickness, bare_length [m] the
length of bare tube between two fins (fin interval minus the fin thickness),
and rho [kg/m^3], Cp [J/kg-K], mu [Pa-s], k [W/m-K], k_fin [W/m-K] the bulk
air and fin properties. eta_f is the fin efficiency of
eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler.
Validity: 1000 < Re < 8000, 11.13 mm < D_tube < 40.89 mm, 1.42 mm < fin height
  < 16.57 mm, 0.33 mm < fin thickness < 2.02 mm, 1.30 mm < fin pitch < 4.06 mm,
  24.49 mm < normal pitch < 111 mm (as in the original).
Original: Briggs, D. E. and E. H. Young, 1963, "Convection Heat Transfer and
  Pressure Drop of Air Flowing across Triangular Banks of Finned Tubes",
  Chemical Engineering Progress Symp., Series 41, No. 59. Chem. Eng. Prog.
  Symp. Series No. 41, "Heat Transfer - Houston"; as given in Mukherjee, R.
  and G. Hewitt, "Practical Thermal Design of Air-Cooled Heat Exchangers",
  Begell House Publishers, 2007, and Kroeger, D., "Air-Cooled Heat Exchangers
  and Cooling Towers: Thermal-Flow Performance Evaluation and Design", Vol. 1,
  PennWell Corp., 2004.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py, h_Briggs_Young,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  fin_height = (fin_diameter - tube_diameter)/2
  V_max = m/(A_min*rho)
  Re = V_max*tube_diameter*rho/mu
  Pr = Cp*mu/k
  Nu = 0.134*Re^0.681*Pr^(1/3)*(bare_length/fin_height)^0.2*(bare_length/fin_thickness)^0.1134
  h = k/tube_diameter*Nu
  efficiency = eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler(tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, k_fin, h)
  h_A_total = (efficiency*A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A*h
  h_Briggs_Young = A_increase*h_A_total
END

FUNCTION h_ESDU_high_fin(m, A, A_min, A_increase, A_fin, A_tube_showing, tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, bare_length, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, tube_rows, rho, Cp, mu, k, k_fin, Pr_wall)
{H_ESDU_HIGH_FIN - air-side heat-transfer coefficient of a high-fin bundle
(fins at least 1/3 in high), as a bare-tube-basis coefficient [W/m^2-K].

  Nu = 0.242 Re^0.658 (S/h_f)^0.297 (p_1/p_2)^-0.091 Pr^(1/3) F_1 F_2

  F_2 = 0.76 (1 row), 0.84 (2 rows), 0.92 (3 rows), 1 (4 rows or more)
  F_1 = (Pr/Pr_wall)^0.26, the wall property correction factor

  V_max = m/(A_min rho),  Re = V_max D_tube rho/mu,  Pr = Cp mu/k
  h = k/D_tube Nu
  h_{A,total} = (eta_f A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A h
  h_{bare,total} = A_increase h_{A,total}

Arguments as in h_Briggs_Young, plus pitch_parallel [m] (distance between tube
centres along a line parallel to the flow), pitch_normal [m] (distance between
tube centres in a line 90 degrees to the flow), tube_rows [-] (number of tube
rows per bundle) and Pr_wall [-] (Prandtl number at the wall temperature).
Passing Pr_wall = Pr gives F_1 = 1, i.e. no property correction: this is what
the original does when its Pr_wall argument is not given. F_2 is 1 for four
tube rows or more.
Validity: none quoted in the original; the data of the ESDU report it is
  taken from cover high fins (4 to 11 fins/inch, tube diameters 3/8 to 2 in,
  fin heights 1/3 to 5/8 in, fin-tip to fin-root diameter ratios 1.2 to 2.4,
  5000 < Re < 50000).
Original: "High-Fin Staggered Tube Banks: Heat Transfer and Pressure Drop for
  Turbulent Single Phase Gas Flow." ESDU 86022 (October 1, 1986); as given in
  Hewitt, G. L. Shires, T. R. Bott G. F., G. L. Shires and T. R. Bott, "Process
  Heat Transfer", 1st edition, CRC Press, 1994.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py, h_ESDU_high_fin,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  fin_height = (fin_diameter - tube_diameter)/2
  V_max = m/(A_min*rho)
  Re = V_max*tube_diameter*rho/mu
  Pr = Cp*mu/k
  Nu = 0.242*Re^0.658*(bare_length/fin_height)^0.297*(pitch_normal/pitch_parallel)^-0.091*Pr^(1/3)
  IF tube_rows < 2 THEN
    F_2 = 0.76
  ELSE
    IF tube_rows < 3 THEN
      F_2 = 0.84
    ELSE
      IF tube_rows < 4 THEN
        F_2 = 0.92
      ELSE
        F_2 = 1
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  Nu = Nu*F_2*(Pr/Pr_wall)^0.26
  h = k/tube_diameter*Nu
  efficiency = eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler(tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, k_fin, h)
  h_A_total = (efficiency*A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A*h
  h_ESDU_high_fin = A_increase*h_A_total
END

FUNCTION h_ESDU_low_fin(m, A, A_min, A_increase, A_fin, A_tube_showing, tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, bare_length, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, tube_rows, rho, Cp, mu, k, k_fin, Pr_wall)
{H_ESDU_LOW_FIN - air-side heat-transfer coefficient of a low-fin bundle (fins
formed on the tube outside wall, normally by cold rolling), as a
bare-tube-basis coefficient [W/m^2-K].

  Nu = 0.183 Re^0.7 (S/h_f)^0.36 (p_1/D_fin)^0.06 (h_f/D_fin)^0.11 Pr^0.36
       F_1 F_2

  F_2 = ESDU tube row count correction factor (in-line or staggered, see the
       table below; 1 for 10 tube rows or more, which disables the correction)
  F_1 = (Pr/Pr_wall)^0.26, the wall property correction factor

  V_max = m/(A_min rho),  Re = V_max D_tube rho/mu,  Pr = Cp mu/k
  h = k/D_tube Nu
  h_{A,total} = (eta_f A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A h
  h_{bare,total} = A_increase h_{A,total}

Arguments as in h_ESDU_high_fin. The bundle is taken as staggered when
|1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel| > 0.05, in-line otherwise. The row count
correction factor F_2 (ESDU 73031, as shown in Hewitt et al.) is written here
as the ladder below, the form of the function ESDU_tube_row_correction of
library model CSL-0095:

  tube rows      staggered    in-line
  2              0.8593       0.8479
  3              0.8593       0.8479
  4              0.8984       0.8957
  5              0.9268       0.9306
  6              0.9482       0.9551
  7              0.9650       0.9724
  8              0.9777       0.9839
  9              0.9868       0.9902
  10 or more     1            1

The original has a third correction factor for tube angles other than 30, 45 or
60 degrees, which is not fully explained and is not shown in the source of the
ESDU relation; it is not implemented here either (as in the original).
Validity: none quoted in the formula; the data of the ESDU report cover low
  fins (11 to 32 fins/inch, tube diameters 0.5 to 1.25 in, fin heights 0.03 to
  0.1 in, 1000 < Re < 80000).
Original: "High-Fin Staggered Tube Banks: Heat Transfer and Pressure Drop for
  Turbulent Single Phase Gas Flow." ESDU 86022 (October 1, 1986); the row
  count factor is from "Convective Heat Transfer During Crossflow of Fluids
  Over Plain Tube Banks." ESDU 73031 (November 1, 1973); both as given in
  Hewitt, G. L. Shires, T. R. Bott G. F., G. L. Shires and T. R. Bott, "Process
  Heat Transfer", 1st edition, CRC Press, 1994.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py, h_ESDU_low_fin
  (which calls ESDU_tube_row_correction of ht/conv_tube_bank.py and
  wall_factor of ht/core.py), MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  fin_height = (fin_diameter - tube_diameter)/2
  V_max = m/(A_min*rho)
  Re = V_max*tube_diameter*rho/mu
  Pr = Cp*mu/k
  Nu = 0.183*Re^0.7*(bare_length/fin_height)^0.36*(pitch_normal/fin_diameter)^0.06*(fin_height/fin_diameter)^0.11*Pr^0.36
  IF ABS(1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel) > 0.05 THEN
    staggered = 1
  ELSE
    staggered = 0
  ENDIF
  F_2 = 1
  IF tube_rows <= 2 THEN
    IF staggered = 1 THEN
      F_2 = 0.8593
    ELSE
      F_2 = 0.8479
    ENDIF
  ELSE
    IF tube_rows < 10 THEN
      IF staggered = 1 THEN
        F_2 = 0.8984
        IF tube_rows = 5 THEN F_2 = 0.9268
        IF tube_rows = 6 THEN F_2 = 0.9482
        IF tube_rows = 7 THEN F_2 = 0.965
        IF tube_rows = 8 THEN F_2 = 0.9777
        IF tube_rows = 9 THEN F_2 = 0.9868
      ELSE
        F_2 = 0.8957
        IF tube_rows = 5 THEN F_2 = 0.9306
        IF tube_rows = 6 THEN F_2 = 0.9551
        IF tube_rows = 7 THEN F_2 = 0.9724
        IF tube_rows = 8 THEN F_2 = 0.9839
        IF tube_rows = 9 THEN F_2 = 0.9902
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  Nu = Nu*F_2*(Pr/Pr_wall)^0.26
  h = k/tube_diameter*Nu
  efficiency = eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler(tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, k_fin, h)
  h_A_total = (efficiency*A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A*h
  h_ESDU_low_fin = A_increase*h_A_total
END

FUNCTION h_Ganguli_VDI(m, A, A_min, A_increase, A_fin, A_tube_showing, tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, bare_length, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, tube_rows, rho, Cp, mu, k, k_fin)
{H_GANGULI_VDI - air-side heat-transfer coefficient of a finned tube bundle, as
a bare-tube-basis coefficient [W/m^2-K]; the Ganguli parametric-study formula as
modified in the VDI Heat Atlas.

  In-line:    Nu_d = 0.22 Re_d^0.6 (A/A_tube,only)^-0.15 Pr^(1/3)
  Staggered:  Nu_d = 0.38 Re_d^0.6 (A/A_tube,only)^-0.15 Pr^(1/3)

The leading coefficient depends on the arrangement and on the row count:
in-line (|1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel| < 0.05) 0.2 for 3 tube rows or
fewer, 0.22 above; staggered 0.2 for 1 row, 0.33 for 2, 0.36 for 3 and 0.38
above. The area ratio is passed as A_increase (the VDI example shows the ratio
of the total area to the original bare-tube area), and

  V_max = m/(A_min rho),  Re = V_max D_tube rho/mu,  Pr = Cp mu/k
  h = k/D_tube Nu
  h_{A,total} = (eta_f A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A h
  h_{bare,total} = A_increase h_{A,total}

Arguments as in h_Briggs_Young, plus pitch_parallel [m], pitch_normal [m] and
tube_rows [-].
Validity: none quoted in the original.
Original: Ganguli, A., S. S. Tung and J. Taborek, "Parametric Study of
  Air-Cooled Heat Exchanger Finned Tube Geometry", in AIChE Symposium Series
  81: 122-128, 1985; as modified in V. D. I. Gesellschaft (ed.), "VDI Heat
  Atlas", 2nd edition, Springer, 2010; the worked example (Example 12.1) of
  Serth, R. W. and T. Lestina, "Process Heat Transfer: Principles, Applications
  and Rules of Thumb", Academic Press, 2014, gives this function; the model is
  also shown in Kroeger, D., "Air-Cooled Heat Exchangers and Cooling Towers",
  Vol. 1, PennWell Corp., 2004.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py, h_Ganguli_VDI,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  V_max = m/(A_min*rho)
  Re = V_max*tube_diameter*rho/mu
  Pr = Cp*mu/k
  IF ABS(1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel) < 0.05 THEN
    IF tube_rows < 4 THEN
      coeff = 0.2
    ELSE
      coeff = 0.22
    ENDIF
  ELSE
    IF tube_rows = 1 THEN
      coeff = 0.2
    ELSE
      IF tube_rows = 2 THEN
        coeff = 0.33
      ELSE
        IF tube_rows = 3 THEN
          coeff = 0.36
        ELSE
          coeff = 0.38
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  Nu = coeff*Re^0.6*Pr^(1/3)*A_increase^-0.15
  h = k/tube_diameter*Nu
  efficiency = eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler(tube_diameter, fin_diameter, fin_thickness, k_fin, h)
  h_A_total = (efficiency*A_fin + A_tube_showing)/A*h
  h_Ganguli_VDI = A_increase*h_A_total
END

FUNCTION dP_ESDU_high_fin(m, A_min, A_increase, flow_area_contraction_ratio, tube_diameter, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, tube_rows, rho, mu)
{DP_ESDU_HIGH_FIN - air-side pressure drop across a high-fin tube bank [Pa],
with the effects of the friction along the fins and of the acceleration.

  V_max = m/(A_min rho),  Re = V_max D_tube rho/mu
  K_f = 4.567 Re^-0.242 A_increase^0.504 (p_1/D_tube)^-0.376
                     (p_2/D_tube)^-0.546
  K_acc = 1 + (flow area contraction ratio)^2
  dP = (K_acc + n_rows K_f) rho V_max^2 / 2

m [kg/s] is the mass flow rate of air, A_min [m^2] the minimum free-flow area,
A_increase [-] the ratio of the actual surface area to the bare-tube surface
area, flow_area_contraction_ratio [-] the ratio of A_min to the bundle face
area, tube_diameter [m] the bare-tube diameter, pitch_parallel [m] and
pitch_normal [m] the tube pitches, tube_rows [-] the number of tube rows, rho
[kg/m^3] the bulk air density and mu [Pa-s] the bulk air viscosity. The
Reynolds number is based on V_max, i.e. on the minimum free-flow area.
Validity: the data of the ESDU report cover fin densities 4 to 11/inch, tube
  outer diameters 3/8 to 2 in, fin heights 1/3 to 5/8 in, fin-tip to
  fin-root diameter ratios 1.2 to 2.4 and 5000 < Re < 50000; the report claims
  72 % of its experimental points within 10 % of this correlation.
Original: "High-Fin Staggered Tube Banks: Heat Transfer and Pressure Drop for
  Turbulent Single Phase Gas Flow." ESDU (October 1, 1986); as described in
  Hewitt, G. L. Shires T. Reg Bott G. F., G. L. Shires and T. R. Bott, "Process
  Heat Transfer", 1st edition, CRC Press, 1994.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py, dP_ESDU_high_fin,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  V_max = m/(A_min*rho)
  Re = V_max*tube_diameter*rho/mu
  K_f = 4.567*Re^-0.242*A_increase^0.504*(pitch_normal/tube_diameter)^-0.376*(pitch_parallel/tube_diameter)^-0.546
  K_acc = 1 + flow_area_contraction_ratio^2
  dP_ESDU_high_fin = (K_acc + tube_rows*K_f)*0.5*rho*V_max^2
END

FUNCTION dP_ESDU_low_fin(m, A_min, A_increase, flow_area_contraction_ratio, tube_diameter, fin_height, bare_length, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, tube_rows, rho, mu)
{DP_ESDU_LOW_FIN - air-side pressure drop across a low-fin tube bank [Pa], with
the effects of the friction along the fins and of the acceleration.

  V_max = m/(A_min rho),  Re = V_max D_tube rho/mu
  K_f = 4.72 Re^-0.286 (h_f/S)^0.51 ((p_1-D_tube)/(p_2-D_tube))^0.536
                     (D_tube/(p_1-D_tube))^0.36
  K_acc = 1 + (flow area contraction ratio)^2
  dP = (K_acc + n_rows K_f) rho V_max^2 / 2

Arguments as in dP_ESDU_high_fin, plus fin_height [m] (the height of the fins
above the bare tube) and bare_length [m] (the length of bare tube between two
fins). The Reynolds number is based on V_max, i.e. on the minimum free-flow
area. Low fins are fins formed on the tube outside wall, normally by the cold
rolling process.
Validity: the data of the ESDU report cover fin densities 11 to 32/inch, tube
  outer diameters 0.5 to 1.25 in, fin heights 0.03 to 0.1 in and
  1000 < Re < 80000; the report compared this correlation with 81 results and
  obtained a standard deviation of 7.7 %.
Original: "High-Fin Staggered Tube Banks: Heat Transfer and Pressure Drop for
  Turbulent Single Phase Gas Flow." ESDU (October 1, 1986); as described in
  Hewitt, G. L. Shires T. Reg Bott G. F., G. L. Shires and T. R. Bott, "Process
  Heat Transfer", 1st edition, CRC Press, 1994.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py, dP_ESDU_low_fin,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  V_max = m/(A_min*rho)
  Re = V_max*tube_diameter*rho/mu
  K_f = 4.72*Re^-0.286*(fin_height/bare_length)^0.51*((pitch_normal-tube_diameter)/(pitch_parallel-tube_diameter))^0.536*(tube_diameter/(pitch_normal-tube_diameter))^0.36
  K_acc = 1 + flow_area_contraction_ratio^2
  dP_ESDU_low_fin = (K_acc + tube_rows*K_f)*0.5*rho*V_max^2
END

FUNCTION air_cooler_noise_GPSA(tip_speed, power)
{AIR_COOLER_NOISE_GPSA - sound pressure level at 1 m from an air-cooler bay
with one fan, GPSA handbook method [dB(A)].

  PWL = 56 + 30 log10(tip speed [m/min]/304.8) + 10 log10(power [hp])

tip_speed [m/s] is the tip speed of the fan blades and power [W] the shaft
power of a single fan motor; the formula uses m/min and hp, so the inputs are
converted here (60 m/min per m/s and 745.6998715822701 W per hp, the values
used by the original library).
Validity: none quoted in the original.
Original: GPSA, "Engineering Data Book, SI", 13th edition, Gas Processors
  Suppliers Association, 2012 (air-cooler design and noise; the example of the
  original library is an example problem of this book).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py,
  air_cooler_noise_GPSA, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  air_cooler_noise_GPSA = 56 + 30*log10(tip_speed*60/304.8) + 10*log10(power/745.6998715822701)
END

FUNCTION air_cooler_noise_Mukherjee(tip_speed, power, fan_diameter, induced)
{AIR_COOLER_NOISE_MUKHERJEE - sound pressure level at 1 m from an air-cooler
bay with one fan (p0 = 2E-5 Pa), Mukherjee and Hewitt method [dB(A)].

  SPL = 46 + 30 log10(tip speed [m/s]) + 10 log10(power [hp])
             - 20 log10(D_fan), less 3 dB for an induced-draft fan

tip_speed [m/s] is the tip speed of the fan blades, power [W] the shaft power
of a single fan motor, fan_diameter [m] the fan diameter and induced [-] 0 for
a forced-draft and 1 for an induced-draft air cooler. The formula uses hp,
so the input is converted here (745.6998715822701 W per hp, the value used by
the original library).
Validity: none quoted in the original.
Original: Mukherjee, R. and G. Hewitt, "Practical Thermal Design of Air-Cooled
  Heat Exchangers", Begell House Publishers Inc., 2007.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/air_cooler.py,
  air_cooler_noise_Mukherjee, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  noise = 46 + 30*log10(tip_speed) + 10*log10(power/745.6998715822701) - 20*log10(fan_diameter)
  IF induced = 1 THEN
    noise = noise - 3
  ENDIF
  air_cooler_noise_Mukherjee = noise
END

"!Demonstration program: every function is called twice"
"It is ignored by the future $INCLUDE library:air_cooler_air_side (CS-FEAT-IMPORT)."
"Case A: the input sets of the ht doctests of each function (three bundles and"
"one fan); case B: a second, uniform set (a two-row in-line low-fin bundle and"
"a second fan). The ht values of both cases are tabulated in the README."

"!Helper functions - modified Bessel functions of the first and second kind (z = 1.5)"
I0_A = bessel_mod_I_series(0, 1.5)
I1_A = bessel_mod_I_series(1, 1.5)
K0_A = bessel_mod_K_series(0, 1.5)
K1_A = bessel_mod_K_series(1, 1.5)

"!Helper function - circular fin efficiency (ht doctest of fin_efficiency_Kern_Kraus)"
eta_fin_doctest = eta_fin_Kern_Kraus_aircooler(0.0254, 0.05715, 3.8E-4, 200, 58)

"!Case A1 - high-fin bundle: 4 rows of 20 tubes, 3 m long, 1 in OD, 0.4 mm fins"
"!at 2.309 mm pitch, 15.9 mm high, staggered pitches 52.07 x 60.33 mm, 21.56 kg/s of air"
m_A1 = 21.56
A_A1 = 452.2258759
A_min_A1 = 1.760309311
A_increase_A1 = 23.61351166
A_fin_A1 = 436.4421443
A_tube_showing_A1 = 15.78373157
tube_diameter_A1 = 0.0254
fin_diameter_A1 = 0.0572
fin_thickness_A1 = 0.000406
bare_length_A1 = 0.001903
pitch_parallel_A1 = 0.05207
pitch_normal_A1 = 0.06033
tube_rows_A1 = 4
rho_A1 = 1.161
Cp_A1 = 1007
mu_A1 = 1.85E-5
k_A1 = 0.0263
k_fin_A1 = 205
Pr_wall_A1 = Cp_A1*mu_A1/k_A1   "Pr_wall = Pr: no property correction, as in the original [1]"

h_Briggs_Young_A1 = h_Briggs_Young(m_A1, A_A1, A_min_A1, A_increase_A1, A_fin_A1, A_tube_showing_A1, tube_diameter_A1, fin_diameter_A1, fin_thickness_A1, bare_length_A1, rho_A1, Cp_A1, mu_A1, k_A1, k_fin_A1)
h_ESDU_high_fin_A1 = h_ESDU_high_fin(m_A1, A_A1, A_min_A1, A_increase_A1, A_fin_A1, A_tube_showing_A1, tube_diameter_A1, fin_diameter_A1, fin_thickness_A1, bare_length_A1, pitch_parallel_A1, pitch_normal_A1, tube_rows_A1, rho_A1, Cp_A1, mu_A1, k_A1, k_fin_A1, Pr_wall_A1)
h_ESDU_high_fin_wall_A1 = h_ESDU_high_fin(m_A1, A_A1, A_min_A1, A_increase_A1, A_fin_A1, A_tube_showing_A1, tube_diameter_A1, fin_diameter_A1, fin_thickness_A1, bare_length_A1, pitch_parallel_A1, pitch_normal_A1, tube_rows_A1, rho_A1, Cp_A1, mu_A1, k_A1, k_fin_A1, 0.71)

"!Case A2 - low-fin bundle: 4 rows of 8 tubes, 0.5 m long, 16.4 mm OD, 1 mm fins"
"!at 3 mm pitch, 4.1 mm high, staggered pitches 27.1 x 31.3 mm, 0.914 kg/s of air"
m_A2 = 0.914
A_A2 = 3.778288765
A_min_A2 = 0.04866666667
A_increase_A2 = 4.583333333
A_fin_A2 = 3.22871949
A_tube_showing_A2 = 0.5495692749
tube_diameter_A2 = 0.0164
fin_diameter_A2 = 0.0246
fin_thickness_A2 = 0.001
bare_length_A2 = 0.002
fin_height_A2 = 0.0041
pitch_parallel_A2 = 0.0271
pitch_normal_A2 = 0.0313
tube_rows_A2 = 4
flow_area_contraction_ratio_A2 = 0.3658460189
rho_A2 = 1.217
Cp_A2 = 1007
mu_A2 = 1.8E-5
k_A2 = 0.0253
k_fin_A2 = 15
Pr_wall_A2 = Cp_A2*mu_A2/k_A2   "Pr_wall = Pr: no property correction, as in the original [1]"

h_ESDU_low_fin_A2 = h_ESDU_low_fin(m_A2, A_A2, A_min_A2, A_increase_A2, A_fin_A2, A_tube_showing_A2, tube_diameter_A2, fin_diameter_A2, fin_thickness_A2, bare_length_A2, pitch_parallel_A2, pitch_normal_A2, tube_rows_A2, rho_A2, Cp_A2, mu_A2, k_A2, k_fin_A2, Pr_wall_A2)
h_ESDU_low_fin_wall_A2 = h_ESDU_low_fin(m_A2, A_A2, A_min_A2, A_increase_A2, A_fin_A2, A_tube_showing_A2, tube_diameter_A2, fin_diameter_A2, fin_thickness_A2, bare_length_A2, pitch_parallel_A2, pitch_normal_A2, tube_rows_A2, rho_A2, Cp_A2, mu_A2, k_A2, k_fin_A2, 0.72)
dP_ESDU_high_fin_A2 = dP_ESDU_high_fin(m_A2, A_min_A2, A_increase_A2, flow_area_contraction_ratio_A2, tube_diameter_A2, pitch_parallel_A2, pitch_normal_A2, tube_rows_A2, rho_A2, mu_A2)
dP_ESDU_low_fin_A2 = dP_ESDU_low_fin(m_A2, A_min_A2, A_increase_A2, flow_area_contraction_ratio_A2, tube_diameter_A2, fin_height_A2, bare_length_A2, pitch_parallel_A2, pitch_normal_A2, tube_rows_A2, rho_A2, mu_A2)

"!Case A3 - Ganguli/VDI worked example (Example 12.1 of Serth and Lestina):"
"!4 rows of 56 tubes, 36 ft long, 1 in OD, 0.33 mm fins at 10/inch, 15.875 mm"
"!high, pitches 63.5 x 110 mm, 130.7 kg/s of air"
m_A3 = 130.70315
A_A3 = 4211.940656
A_min_A3 = 20.87531309
A_increase_A3 = 21.475
A_fin_A3 = 4041.305575
A_tube_showing_A3 = 170.6350813
tube_diameter_A3 = 0.0254
fin_diameter_A3 = 0.05715
fin_thickness_A3 = 0.0003302
